They were translated from TOML to JSON verbatim (no rule content touched) for
this plugin's pure-standard-library runtime engine. Each snapshot's upstream
commit is recorded in detection/UPSTREAM.json. The full Apache License 2.0
text lives in LICENSE.

herdr ships nothing for the deepseek harness (dsh). detection/dsh-tui.json is
original work (NOT derived from herdr) covering the dsh TUI interface, and is
licensed Apache-2.0 with the rest of this repository. dsh interfaces can also
self-report state through scripts/agent-state.sh; that override outranks the
screen-scrape rules.
